      "title": "Match a request to its resource policy",
      "eyebrow": "Learn",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "A resource-based policy is attached to a resource and specifies the principals, actions and resources covered by its statements.",
          "role": "definition",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.evaluate_resource_based_permissions_for_a_requested_operation"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.evaluate_resource_based_permissions_for_a_requested_operation#tb1",
              "aws_devops.evaluate_resource_based_permissions_for_a_requested_operation#tb2"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.evaluate_resource_based_permissions_for_a_requested_operation#f1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "For an S3 bucket policy, compare Principal, Action, Resource and Condition with the request. Bucket and object ARNs have different scopes. Same-account identity and resource permissions can contribute allows; applicable explicit denies override them. Cross-account access generally requires permission on both sides.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.evaluate_resource_based_permissions_for_a_requested_operation"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.evaluate_resource_based_permissions_for_a_requested_operation#tb3"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.evaluate_resource_based_permissions_for_a_requested_operation#f2",
              "aws_devops.evaluate_resource_based_permissions_for_a_requested_operation#f3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
